            <div xml:id="d683">

                <pb facs="0939" n="825" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg825"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890h.01/12: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dawes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-15T16:00:00+00:00">April 15, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 15—1:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>109. Embassy’s despatch 1622, February 3.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d683-f1"/> I have
                    learned informally that the Afghan Minister desires to call on me in the near
                    future to discuss the question of recognition.</p>
                <p>Unless otherwise instructed I propose to receive him and to say only that I will
                    report the matter to my Government. An expression of the Department’s views
                    would be appreciated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
